# WeWatch Project Rules

## �‍💻 About the Creator

**Chibuzor (chibuzor_dev)** - Founder & Lead Developer of WeWatch

WeWatch represents the culmination of months of intense development, learning, and iteration. This project has been built from the ground up with a vision to revolutionize social video watching and create a platform where creators and communities can thrive together.

**Journey Highlights:**
- Started as a simple watch party concept, evolved into a full social platform
- Overcame countless technical challenges: WebRTC audio routing, 3D rendering, real-time sync
- Built complete monetization ecosystem (tokens, gifts, ads) from scratch
- Mastered full-stack development: Go backend, React frontend, PostgreSQL, WebSockets, LiveKit
- Implemented complex features: LiveShare graphics, quiz system, games, recording capabilities
- Maintained laser focus on user experience and creator-first design
- Prepared for launch with production-ready security, logging, and scalability

**Technical Stack Mastery:**
- Backend: Go (Gin), GORM, PostgreSQL, WebSockets, JWT auth
- Frontend: React, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Three.js (3D rendering)
- Infrastructure: LiveKit (audio/video), Stripe (payments), Cloudflare R2 (storage)
- Real-time: WebSocket architecture, binary protocols, state synchronization

This is more than a project - it's a testament to perseverance, continuous learning, and the belief that great products come from deeply understanding both technology and user needs.

