## 📍 PROJECT STATUS (June 23, 2026 - DEVICE STREAMING PHASE 19: FIXED LATE-JOINER URL + ORPHANED PREVIEW TICKER)

### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 23, 2026, newest of all):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 19 (complete)** ✅
- User asked two forward-looking questions before further testing: does the lobby preview update correctly when the host switches from a device-stream upload to LiveShare/Watch-From mid-session, and would a late joiner (relying on `session_status`, not the `device_stream_ready` broadcast) see what the host sees with no sync issues?
- Bug 1, more serious than expected: late joiners got a fundamentally broken media URL, not just an out-of-sync one. `current_media_url` is stored as a relative `/uploads/...` path by both upload pipelines, and flows untouched into the late-join restoration effect — unlike every other path in the file (`device_stream_ready`'s own handler, `handlePlayMedia`, etc.), which all resolve it against the backend's origin first. A late joiner's browser was resolving it against the *frontend's* origin instead — a guaranteed 404. Fixed by extracting one shared `resolveMediaUrl()` helper, used at all five places in `VideoWatch.jsx` that had been duplicating this same resolution logic.
- Bug 2: switching from a device-stream upload to LiveShare/Watch-From never told the backend the media type changed — `watch_sessions.current_media_type` stayed `"upload"` forever, and the preview-refresh ticker (Phase 17) kept running indefinitely against the old, possibly-deleted upload, periodically overwriting the fresh LiveShare poster with stale content. The backend already has the right teardown (`update_media_state`/`screen_share_started` WS handlers correctly call `ClearOldPreview`) but cinema rooms never sent either message type — only `LectureHallPage.jsx`/`PositionCalculatorPage.jsx` did. Fixed by sending `update_media_state` from `handleStartLiveShare` and `handleEndScreenShare`.
- Verified for real: a two-account late-join test confirmed the joiner got a genuine playing `blob:` video (proof the manifest fetch succeeded against the correct origin) landing within ~2.5s of the host's actual position, then continuing smoothly. For the ticker fix — LiveKit isn't available in this dev environment to drive the real UI button — verified by sending the exact WS payload the new code constructs against a session whose ticker had been confirmed firing every ~60s for 18+ minutes straight; confirmed type-change detection, preview clearing, and the next two naturally-due ticks never firing.
- Full technical detail in `CLAUDE.md` under "Device Streaming via HLS → Phase 19."

