## 📍 PROJECT STATUS (June 22, 2026 - DEVICE STREAMING PHASE 16: CHUNK UPLOADS SURVIVE AN EXPIRED TOKEN)

### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 22, 2026, newest of all):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 16 (complete)** ✅
- User hit "failed to upload chunks" after a system restart. Root-caused as a genuine JWT expiry (7-day lifetime, token expired 22 seconds before the request per exact Unix math) — confirmed not caused by any Phase 14/15 change (no auth files touched, no stale duplicate backend process).
- Found the real, fixable gap alongside it: `uploadChunk` used a raw `axios.post` instead of the shared `apiClient` instance, bypassing the app's existing auto-refresh-on-401 interceptor that every other API call already benefits from — so an expired token here just failed outright instead of silently refreshing and retrying.
- Fixed by switching to `apiClient.post(...)`, plus one supporting change: the request interceptor no longer unconditionally overwrites an already-set `Authorization` header (needed so the refresh-retry's fresh token survives being re-sent through the same interceptor on retry).
- Verified for real: registered a fresh test account, poisoned its stored token with garbage, ran a real chunked upload through the actual UI — confirmed the very first chunk attempt succeeded (refresh-and-retry happened transparently inside it) and the stored token afterward was a genuine fresh JWT.
- Full technical detail in `CLAUDE.md` under "Device Streaming via HLS → Phase 16."

