## 📍 PROJECT STATUS (June 22, 2026 - DEVICE STREAMING PHASE 15: PLAYLIST CLEANUP + PREVIEW REFRESH FOR CINEMA ROOMS)

### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 22, 2026, newer than the latest of the latest):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 15 (complete)** ✅
- Finished playlist items are now always removed, even the last one — previously only items with a *next* item to advance to got removed; the last one just cleared "Playing Now" but stayed visible, dead and unclickable (re-selecting it doesn't restart it — the player only reloads on an actual media change, not a re-select of the same item). One-line fix: moved the playlist filter outside the if/else in `handleVideoEnd`. Still local/per-client only, same as before.
- Session preview refresh (1m dev / 5m prod) now applies to cinema/video-watch rooms — previously the refresh ticker only ever started via a `media_play` WS message that's exclusively sent from classroom/lecture-hall pages, so cinema rooms got exactly one preview at upload time and never another. New `startSessionPreviewRefresh` persists the same session fields `HandleMediaPlay` already writes for classroom and starts the existing ticker directly, called from both the progressive and fallback upload paths.
- Found a real bug while wiring this up: the existing flat-file refresh path would have silently misbehaved for any `IsStream: true` item — and testing showed that's nearly every video/audio upload, not just progressive ones, since the fallback path HLS-ifies almost everything regardless of pipeline. Branched `refreshPreview` on `IsStream` to route stream items through a new HLS-segment-aware callback instead, using the freshest available segments each refresh (not just replaying the same opening few seconds) and overwriting the same deterministic filename in place.
- Verified for real: let a progressive upload's ticker run un-ended for an extended period, confirmed dozens of on-schedule refreshes, then confirmed session-end correctly stopped it (zero further refreshes after the end call). Also verified a guaranteed-fallback-pipeline tiny file — confirmed it also came back `IsStream: true` and refreshed correctly via the same path.
- Full technical detail in `CLAUDE.md` under "Device Streaming via HLS → Phase 15."

