## 📍 PROJECT STATUS (June 22, 2026 - DEVICE STREAMING PHASE 14: SWEEP-GAP FIXES, DEAD-ITEM AUTO-REMOVAL, ANIMATED PREVIEWS)

### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 22, 2026, the latest of the latest):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 14 (complete)** ✅
- Fixed the two real sweep-function gaps from the Phase 13 incident write-up: `CleanupAllTemporaryMedia` and `DeleteTemporaryMediaItemsForRoomHandler` both skipped the DB row delete entirely when the file delete failed — removed the `continue` in both so the row always gets deleted regardless. Verified with a genuine permission-denied failure (a nonexistent file doesn't count — `DeleteMediaFile` treats that as success) via a standalone, since-deleted test program: confirmed the row was removed despite the file-delete failure being logged.
- Dead playlist items now auto-remove instead of erroring forever: `VideoWatch.jsx`'s error handler detects hls.js's fatal `manifestLoadError` specifically, removes the item locally, shows a toast instead of a blocking alert, and (host-only) calls the existing delete-item API to purge it for real. Found and fixed a second, unrelated bug while wiring this up — the backend's room broadcast for item deletion was commented out, so even the pre-existing manual "delete" button never synced to other members in real time. Verified end-to-end with a real upload, a narrowly-scoped deletion of just that one upload's directory, and a forced reload that reproduced the exact `manifestLoadError` — confirmed the item vanished from the DOM and the DB row was genuinely soft-deleted.
- Animated session previews (the looping video clip, not just the static poster) now generate for progressive/device-stream uploads too — previously only the poster was fixed in Phase 13. New `GeneratePreviewMP4FromHLSSegments` concatenates the first few HLS segments and re-encodes a 15s/540p clip. Found and fixed a real bug along the way: probing resolution directly against a raw `.ts` segment failed because ffprobe printed the same resolution twice (a transport-stream PAT/PMT quirk) — fixed by taking only the first line of output. No frontend changes needed; the lobby's existing broadcast handler already supported this shape. Verified with `ffprobe` against the real generated file and a direct DB check.
- Full technical detail in `CLAUDE.md` under "Device Streaming via HLS → Phase 14."

