## 📍 PROJECT STATUS (June 22, 2026 - DEVICE STREAMING PHASE 12: FIXED BLACK CLIENT-CAPTURED POSTERS)

### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 22, 2026, most latest):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 12 (complete)** ✅
- User reported the "Playing Now"/playlist poster was black for 2 different files. Root-caused as a real, intermittent race in `captureClientPosterFromFile` (Phase 9): the video's `seeked` event can fire before the browser actually decodes/paints the frame, so the canvas grab sometimes captures a stale black frame. Proved it empirically by scanning poster files already on disk from earlier sessions — found a handful near-zero brightness alongside mostly-correct ones, from the *exact same source file*, confirming pure timing, not content.
- First attempted fix (`requestVideoFrameCallback`, the API built for "frame ready to composite") turned out unreliable — built a standalone Playwright test harness and confirmed its callback never fires at all for a paused/seeked (non-playing) video in this environment. Removed it; kept only a double `requestAnimationFrame` after `seeked`, which reliably works. Also hardened the capture: `preload` changed to `'auto'`, video briefly attached off-screen to the DOM instead of fully detached.
- Verified at volume given the bug was intermittent: 80/80 clean captures across two harder test videos (large-GOP + high-motion) via the standalone harness, plus 2 real end-to-end uploads through the actual app confirming healthy, non-black poster files on disk.
- Full technical detail in `CLAUDE.md` under "Device Streaming via HLS → Phase 12."

