## 📍 PROJECT STATUS (June 22, 2026 - DEVICE STREAMING PHASE 11: MERGED STREAM-FROM-DEVICE INTO BROWSE FILES)

### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 22, 2026, even more latest):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 11 (complete)** ✅
- Confirmed "Stream from Device" and "Browse Files" already ran the identical upload pipeline — the only difference was one flag (`pendingAutoPlayRef.current = true`) the first button set before opening the file picker. Removed "Stream from Device" entirely; folded that flag-set into "Browse Files" unconditionally, so picking any file (including images/PDFs) now auto-displays it for the room, same as the deleted button already did.
- Renamed the button's own "Uploading..." label to "Loading..." — "uploading" wrongly implied the whole transfer had to finish before anything useful happened.
- Fixed a real UX gap: the load bar used to stay visible for the *entire* chunk-sending duration, even after `device_stream_ready` had already started playback partway through a large upload. Added `upload_id` to both backend `device_stream_ready` broadcasts; the upload hook now tracks its own current `upload_id` and hides the bar specifically when its own stream is confirmed ready — `uploading` itself stays `true` the whole time (preserving the button's disabled state and all retry/resume logic), only the visual bar hides early.
- Verified with real network throttling (~5 Mbps, applied only after the app had already loaded): the bar disappeared in the exact poll tick `device_stream_ready` fired, then stayed hidden for 10+ seconds while the button still read "Loading..." — proof the background upload was still genuinely running underneath. An unthrottled localhost run showed why throttling was necessary: the whole 39MB upload finished before ffmpeg could even produce 2 segments, making the fix impossible to observe without it.
- Full technical detail in `CLAUDE.md` under "Device Streaming via HLS → Phase 11."

