## 📍 PROJECT STATUS (June 22, 2026 - DEVICE STREAMING PHASE 10: FIX REDUNDANT RESTARTS + PREP UX)

### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 22, 2026):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 10 (complete)** ✅
- Manual testing of a real 39.5MB/79-chunk upload surfaced "restarts playback 2 times then begins playing" — root-caused as two separate, real bugs from the user's own pasted console log: (1) `LeftSidebar.jsx`'s upload-complete auto-play effect redundantly re-selects the same item `device_stream_ready` already started playing, and (2) Phase 8's own poster/duration fix (`{...prev, poster_url}`) produces a new object reference that `CinemaVideoPlayer.jsx`'s media-load effect (depending on the whole `mediaItem` object) treated as "new media," reloading from scratch. Fixed #1 by checking `currentMedia?.ID` before re-selecting; fixed #2 by narrowing the effect's dependencies to the specific fields it actually reads (`mediaUrl`, `type`, `stream`, `cameraStream`) instead of the whole object.
- Answered directly: yes, "Stream from Device" and "Browse Files" share the same upload state by design — confirmed "Browse Files shows Uploading" is just that button's own label reacting to the same shared `uploading` flag, not a separate stuck indicator.
- Investigated the "stuck at Uploading, 0%, 0B" report and found it isn't a bug — a `useEffect`-based state logger (not a log inside the async upload function itself, which would have hit a real stale-closure trap) confirmed the full `isPreparing → uploading → progress → reset` lifecycle works correctly on a real 39MB upload. Most likely explanation: a normal "just started" moment, made easier to misread given Phase 9's new client-capture delay.
- Added a genuine fix for that delay: new `isPreparing` state shows "Preparing your stream..." during the client-side duration/poster capture window (which sets nothing previously, leaving the UI blank for a few real seconds on a large file) — distinct from the real upload progress bar, never shown simultaneously.
- Full technical detail in `CLAUDE.md` under "Device Streaming via HLS → Phase 10."

