### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 21, 2026, even later):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 7 (complete)** ✅
- Manual testing found progressive HLS uploads always got a hardcoded generic placeholder poster, never a real thumbnail — unlike the fallback path, which already extracts a real frame. Fixed by extracting a real frame from the first HLS segment (`seg_000.ts` — already complete and safely readable the moment the stream is announced ready) instead of the placeholder, mirroring the fallback path's existing `ExtractThumbnail` + CDN-upload + broadcast pattern exactly, in its own goroutine so it never delays the `device_stream_ready` broadcast.
