## 📍 PROJECT STATUS (June 21, 2026 - DEVICE STREAMING PHASE 5: FORMAT COVERAGE AUDIT)

### ✅ LATEST UPDATES (June 21, 2026, even later):

**Device Streaming via HLS — Phase 5 (complete)** ✅
- Audited every video/audio format the file picker advertises (`.mp4/.mov/.m4v/.m4a/.3gp/.webm/.ts/.mkv/.avi/.wmv`) with real files, real uploads, real playback — not assumptions. Result: **every one of them works**, no "can't stream this format" gate was needed at all.
- Found and fixed 3 real bugs that were silently breaking 4 of those formats: `getMimeType()` had no mapping for `.3gp`/`.ts`/`.m4v`/`.wmv` (all fell through to `application/octet-stream`, failing every gate); and a genuinely surprising one — on this Linux test environment, `.ts` files get reported by the browser as `text/vnd.trolltech.linguist` (a Qt Linguist translation format that also uses `.ts`), which the frontend's validation gate then correctly-but-wrongly rejected. Fixed by trusting a known-good extension over a present-but-wrong browser-reported type, since the backend already re-derives the real type from the extension anyway.
- Corrected something said in an earlier conversation: MKV does **not** need transcoding for browser compatibility in the device-streaming path specifically — that concern only applies to the separate, non-streaming permanent-upload path. A progressive MKV upload never reaches `TranscodeMkvToMp4IfNeeded` at all; confirmed with a real test file that MKV's own structure lets the existing probe succeed immediately (prefix=1 chunk), no new code needed.
- One real, secondary finding for a future pass (not chased further now): the "auto-play immediately after upload" convenience feature didn't visibly fire for any of the three fallback-path (non-progressive) test formats within a 40-second window, even though manually clicking the resulting item always played instantly. Narrow gap, doesn't block anything, worth a closer look later.
- Full technical detail in `CLAUDE.md` under "Device Streaming via HLS → Phase 5" — canonical reference, not duplicated here.

