### ✅ PREVIOUS UPDATES (May 8, 2026):

**Notification Enforcement Implemented:**
- ✅ **Settings Now Enforced**: Notification preferences checked before sending WebSocket messages
- ✅ **Master Toggle**: `push_enabled` blocks ALL notifications when disabled
- ✅ **Individual Toggles Respected**: friend_requests_notif, messages_notif, calls_notif now actually work
- ✅ **Privacy vs Notifications**: Privacy settings control access (who_can_*), notification settings control pings
- ✅ **Clear Logging**: Backend logs "🔕 User X has Y notifications disabled" when blocked
- ✅ **Call Cleanup**: If calls_notif disabled, call state cleaned up and caller notified
- ✅ **Zero Breaking Changes**: Uses existing user_settings table, no migration needed
- ✅ **Immediate Effect**: Changes take effect instantly (no app restart)

**Enforced Notification Types:**
1. **Friend Requests** - `friend_requests_notif` checked in friendships.go (2 locations)
2. **Friend Request Accepted** - Same check for acceptance notifications
3. **Incoming Calls** - `calls_notif` checked in lobby_calls.go (prevents wasted call attempts)
4. **Private Messages** - `messages_notif` checked in websocket.go (sender still sees message)

**Not Yet Enforced (Pending Implementation):**
- Session Invites (`session_invites_notif`) - will add when session invite feature is built
- Likes & Comments (`likes_comments_notif`) - will add when post activity notifications are built

**Technical Implementation:**
```go
// Before: Always sent notifications (settings ignored)
hub.BroadcastToUsers([]uint{recipientID}, OutgoingMessage{...})

// After: Checks settings first
var settings models.UserSettings
if err := DB.Where("user_id = ?", recipientID).First(&settings).Error; err == nil {
    if settings.PushEnabled && settings.FriendRequestsNotif {
        hub.BroadcastToUsers([]uint{recipientID}, OutgoingMessage{...})
    } else {
        log.Printf("🔕 User %d has notifications disabled", recipientID)
    }
}
```

**Files Modified (3):**
1. `backend/internal/handlers/friendships.go` - Added friend_requests_notif checks
2. `backend/internal/handlers/lobby_calls.go` - Added calls_notif check with call cleanup
3. `backend/internal/handlers/websocket.go` - Added messages_notif check for private messages
4. `NOTIFICATION_ENFORCEMENT.md` - Full documentation and testing guide

**Benefits:**
- Users can disable notifications without losing functionality
- Better battery life (fewer WebSocket messages)
- Respects user preferences (app store compliance)
- Clear debugging logs (know exactly why notifications aren't arriving)

---

**KYC Auto-Approval System Implemented:**
- ✅ **Auto-Approval on Submission**: KYC instantly approved when user submits documents - no manual review needed
- ✅ **Full Name Field Added**: Users enter legal name (e.g., "Chibuzor") - displayed in admin dashboard
- ✅ **Edit Name Endpoint**: PUT /api/kyc/:kycId to update full_name (fix typos, shorten name)
- ✅ **User Model Denormalization**: kyc_status, kyc_verified_at, kyc_expires_at fields for fast withdrawal checks
- ✅ **2-Year Expiration**: Auto-calculated on approval, expires 2 years after submission
- ✅ **Instant Withdrawals**: Users can withdraw immediately after KYC submission (no waiting for admin)
- ✅ **Admin Dashboard Preserved**: Still functional for spot checks, manual rejection of fraud
- ✅ **Audit Logging**: All KYC actions logged (submission, approval, rejection) with IP/timestamp
- ✅ **Database Migrations**: Two migrations added (kyc_status to users, full_name to kyc_verifications)
- ✅ **Zero Manual Work**: Auto-approve strategy = scalable, better UX, no bottleneck on admin time
- ✅ **Vercel Compatible**: All backend routes work on Railway, frontend displays KYC status correctly

**KYC System Technical Details:**
```go
// Auto-approval happens immediately on submission
Status: "pending" → "approved" (instant)
ExpiresAt: NOW() + 2 years
VerifiedByUserID: NULL (system approved, not admin)
User.KYCStatus: "approved"
User.CanWithdraw(): true

// Fast withdrawal checks (no JOIN)
if user.IsKYCVerified() {
    processWithdrawal() // Instant
}
```

**Why Auto-Approve Works:**
- Most users are legitimate (< 1% fraud rate expected)
- Better UX: Instant withdrawals vs 24-48 hour wait
- Scalable: No admin bottleneck as platform grows
- Standard practice: Nigerian fintechs (Kuda, PiggyVest) use this approach
- Reversible: Can manually reject fraudulent KYCs after the fact
- Spot checks: Admin reviews 5-10% random sample for quality control

**Files Modified (8):**
1. `backend/internal/models/user.go` - Added kyc_status, kyc_verified_at, kyc_expires_at fields + IsKYCVerified() helper
2. `backend/internal/models/kyc_verification.go` - Added full_name field (user's legal name)
3. `backend/internal/handlers/kyc_handlers.go` - Auto-approval logic, UpdateKYCHandler for name edits
4. `backend/cmd/server/main.go` - Added PUT /api/kyc/:kycId route
5. `backend/migrations/20260508000001_add_kyc_status_to_users.sql` - User table migration
6. `backend/migrations/20260508000002_add_full_name_to_kyc.sql` - KYC table migration
7. `KYC_SYSTEM_COMPLETE.md` - Full documentation of manual KYC system
8. `KYC_AUTO_APPROVE.md` - Auto-approval strategy and safety features

**Next: Large Withdrawal Review**
- Auto-approve all KYCs (instant)
- Manual review only for withdrawals > ₦100,000
- Random spot checks on 5-10% of approved KYCs

