### **Target Market:**
- Nigerian users (Lagos, Abuja, Port Harcourt)
- University students (watch parties, study sessions)
- Church communities (live sermons, Bible studies)
- Content creators (podcasts, interviews, live shows)
- Remote teams (watch parties, presentations)

### **Network Effect Strategy:**
- Church mode for viral growth (pastors invite congregations)
- Room-based community building (persistent chat, scheduled events)
- Token economy encourages engagement (gifting, tipping, tickets)

### **Revenue Streams (VERIFIED & CORRECTED May 10, 2026):**
1. **Token Spread Profit (PRIMARY)**: ₦43 per token (26% margin) - Buy ₦165, Withdraw ₦122 ✅
   - Host gets 100% of tokens when users spend on tickets ✅
   - Platform profit realized on buy/sell spread (not on spending)
   - Token valuation for analytics: ₦122 (withdrawal rate, not ₦140.25)
2. **In-Session Donation Fee**: 15% of token donations during watch sessions ✅
   - Intentionally different from ticket commission (donations are voluntary)
3. **Wallet Gift Fee**: 5% of wallet-to-wallet token transfers ✅
4. **Ticket Transfer Fee**: 5% of gifted tickets (separate from ticket price) ✅
5. **Gateway Payment Commission**: 25% on Stripe/Paystack payments (tickets & donations) ✅
   - Corrected from 15% to 25% (consistent 75%/25% split)
6. **Future**: Ads (post-launch), premium subscriptions, recording fees

**Revenue Split Model (CORRECTED May 10, 2026)**:
- **Gateway Tickets/Donations**: 75% Host / 25% Platform
- **Token Tickets**: 100% tokens to Host (platform profits from spread)
- **Token Donations**: 85% to Host / 15% Platform (different from tickets)
- **Ticket Gifting**: 95% to Recipient / 5% Platform
- **Payout Conversion**: Tokens → NGN at ₦122 withdrawal rate

**Test Results** (test-payment-system.sh):
- ✅ 24/25 automated tests passed (96% pass rate)
- ✅ All revenue split logic verified in codebase
- ✅ Payment routes registered: /tokens/purchase, /tickets/purchase, /donate, /gift, /payouts
- ✅ Database schema complete: users, user_wallets, token_transactions, session_tickets, donations, payouts, gateway_earnings, platform_accounting
- ✅ API performance baseline: < 100ms response time

### **🔐 Security Status (April 23, 2026):**

**✅ IMPLEMENTED SECURITY MEASURES:**
- **Password Hashing**: bcrypt with cost factor 12 (strong)
- **JWT Authentication**: 64-char secret, 24-hour token expiry, HS256 signing
- **Rate Limiting**: Auth endpoints limited to 5 attempts/minute per IP
- **Database SSL**: Conditional SSL (required for Railway production, disabled for local dev)
- **Age Verification**: COPPA compliance (13+ years old requirement)
- **Token Storage**: JWT in localStorage, WebSocket token in sessionStorage
- **Environment Variables**: .env in .gitignore, secrets not committed to Git
- **API Key Protection**: All payment/SMTP keys stored in environment variables

**⚠️ KNOWN SECURITY GAPS (Post-Launch Priority):**
- No CORS whitelist (currently allows all origins with patterns - allows localhost, Vercel, Cloudflare Tunnel)
- No session invalidation on logout (JWT remains valid until 24h expiry)
- No account lockout after failed login attempts (rate limiting exists but no permanent lockout)
- No 2FA/MFA option for sensitive actions (withdrawals, password changes)
- No SQL query logging for audit trail (GORM protects against SQL injection, admin actions now audited)
- No Content Security Policy (CSP) headers (XSS protection not enforced)
- No automated dependency vulnerability scanning (no CI/CD security checks)

**🎯 POST-LAUNCH SECURITY ROADMAP:**
- **Week 1**: Implement CORS whitelist, add logout token blacklist
- **Week 2**: ~~Add account lockout (5 failed attempts)~~, ~~SQL audit logging~~ ✅ Admin audit logging implemented
- **Week 3**: Implement CSP headers, dependency scanning (npm audit, go list)
- **Month 2**: Add 2FA option (SMS/email), encrypt sensitive payment data
- **Month 3**: Security audit, penetration testing

