**PHASE 2: Frontend Member State Update (Critical Bug)**

**Issue 2**: Member receives layout broadcast but doesn't render split-view
- **Evidence from Logs**:
  - ✅ Backend: `📡 Broadcasting layout: split-view`
  - ✅ Member: `🎨 Setting layout from broadcast: split-view`
  - ✅ Member: `📹 Camera stream ready: MediaStream`
  - ✅ Member: `🎥 Screen stream ready: MediaStream`
  - ❌ Member: Only screen displays (no split-view)

**Root Cause**: TODO comments in track subscription handlers
- **Location**: `frontend/src/components/cinema/VideoWatch.jsx` (Lines 1050-1110)
- **Problem**: Member logged both camera and screen streams but NEVER called `setCurrentMedia` to pass them to CinemaVideoPlayer
- **Before (Broken)**:
```javascript
// Screen share track subscription (member side)
if (publication.source === Track.Source.ScreenShare) {
  console.log('🎥 Screen stream ready:', screenStream);
  console.log('📹 Camera stream ready:', cameraStream);
  // TODO: Update state to display screen share stream
  return; // ❌ Returns without setting state!
}
```

**Fix 3: Member State Update** - `frontend/src/components/cinema/VideoWatch.jsx` (Lines 1064-1107)
```javascript
// Screen share track subscription (member side)
if (publication.source === Track.Source.ScreenShare) {
  const screenStream = new MediaStream([track.mediaStreamTrack]);
  const cameraTrackPub = participant.getTrackPublication(Track.Source.Camera);
  let cameraStream = null;
  if (cameraTrackPub && cameraTrackPub.track) {
    cameraStream = new MediaStream([cameraTrackPub.track.mediaStreamTrack]);
  }
  
  // ✅ FIXED: Set currentMedia with both streams
  setCurrentMedia({ 
    type: 'liveshare', 
    title: 'LiveShare',
    stream: screenStream,
    cameraStream: cameraStream
  });
  setIsPlaying(true);
  setIsScreenSharingActive(true);
  return;
}

// Camera track subscription (member side)
if (publication.source === Track.Source.Camera) {
  const cameraStream = new MediaStream([track.mediaStreamTraTrack]);
  const screenTrackPub = participant.getTrackPublication(Track.Source.ScreenShare);
  let screenStream = null;
  if (screenTrackPub && screenTrackPub.track) {
    screenStream = new MediaStream([screenTrackPub.track.mediaStreamTrack]);
  }
  
  // ✅ FIXED: Set currentMedia when camera arrives
  if (screenStream) {
    setCurrentMedia({ 
      type: 'liveshare', 
      title: 'LiveShare',
      stream: screenStream,
      cameraStream: cameraStream
    });
    setIsPlaying(true);
    setIsScreenSharingActive(true);
  }
  return;
}
```
- **Result**: CinemaVideoPlayer now receives both streams, calculates `hasBothStreams=true`, renders split-view ✅

