## 🛠️ Discover Feed, Posts Grid, Follow Button & Avatar System (May 11, 2026)

### Architectural Decisions

**Follow model = "join host's main room"**
- "Follow @user" means join `users.main_room_id`. There is no separate `user_follows` table by design.
- A user's follower count = unique members across all rooms they host (see `GetFollowersCountHandler` in `friendships.go`).
- Rooms are the interactive surface for creator-audience engagement; flat follower lists would duplicate the 1:1 friends-chat feature.
- **Don't propose decoupling** (introducing a `user_follows` table or `/follow` endpoint).
- Effective room for a post = `post.room_id ?? post.user.main_room_id`. Posts inherit the author's main room when no explicit room is set.
- A user with no `main_room_id` is intentionally not followable — they need to create or have a room first.

**Avatar URL resolution layer (new — adopt for all new avatar rendering)**
- `frontend/src/utils/avatar.js` — single `resolveAvatarUrl()` helper. Rules:
  - empty / null → frontend-served default silhouette (`/icons/user1avatar.svg`)
  - absolute URL (`http://` / `https://`, includes BunnyCDN) → returned as-is
  - backend path (`/uploads/...`) → prefixed with `VITE_API_BASE_URL`
  - anything else (incl. legacy `/avatars/default.png`) → frontend default
- `frontend/src/components/Avatar.jsx` — drop-in `<Avatar user={...} />` wrapper. Uses the helper and an `onError` fallback (guarded against infinite loops with `dataset.fallback`).
- Backend stores **either** an absolute CDN URL or a relative `/uploads/...` path in `users.avatar_url`. New users have an empty string (the gorm default `/avatars/default.png` was removed because that path was never served).
- **BunnyCDN compatibility:** absolute URLs pass through every layer unchanged — Railway/Vercel deployments using BunnyCDN keep working with no extra code.
- **Field-name mismatch gotcha:** the `/api/friends` endpoint returns `profile_picture` (full URL, built server-side); the raw User model serializes `avatar_url`. The Avatar component accepts either via `user?.avatar_url || user?.profile_picture`.

### Bug Fixes Shipped

- ✅ **DiscoverFeed follow button missing** — frontend was gating the Follow button on `post.room_id` only. Now falls back to `post.user.main_room_id`. Files: `frontend/src/components/DiscoverFeed.jsx`.
- ✅ **`posts.room_id` backfill (16 rows)** — older posts pre-dated the `CreatePost` auto-assign-main-room logic. Backfill SQL: `UPDATE posts p SET room_id = u.main_room_id FROM users u WHERE p.user_id = u.id AND p.room_id IS NULL AND u.main_room_id IS NOT NULL`.
- ✅ **`users.main_room_id` backfill (4 users)** — users with hosted rooms but no main room got their oldest hosted room assigned. Run script in psql when needed.
- ✅ **DiscoverFeed pagination contract** — frontend was sending `?page=N&limit=12` but `GetDiscoverFeed` reads `offset` (silently ignored `page`), causing duplicate page-1 fetches forever. Frontend now sends `offset = (page-1)*PAGE_SIZE`.
- ✅ **DiscoverFeed observer never attached** — observer `useEffect` ran on mount while the loading skeleton was rendered, before the trigger sentinel existed in the DOM. Added `loading` to the dep array so it re-runs after the skeleton is replaced.
- ✅ **`hasMore` flipped false too early** — was `newPosts.length === PAGE_SIZE`. Backend's per-post privacy filter (`GetDiscoverFeed` filters after `LIMIT`) can return short pages, plus visible-set may be smaller than total (soft-deletes). Now `hasMore = newPosts.length > 0` (one extra empty roundtrip at end of feed is acceptable).
- ✅ **PostsGrid same pagination/observer fixes** — plus fixed a broken `fetchPosts(nextPage, filter, true)` call where `filter` was undefined.
- ✅ **PostsGrid observer in scrollable modal** — `UserProfileModal` and `RoomPageEditModal` render `PostsGrid` inside `overflow-y-auto` containers. IntersectionObserver default root is viewport, so inner-container scrolls never fired. Fix: walk up from the trigger to find the nearest scrollable ancestor and pass as `root`. Falls back to viewport when there isn't one.
- ✅ **Chat tab friend avatars** — was reading `friend.avatar_url` (undefined on the `/api/friends` response shape). Fixed to use `friend.profile_picture || friend.avatar_url` with an `onError` fallback to `/icons/user1avatar.svg`.
- ✅ **Avatar URL `/avatars/default.png` 404** — backend prepended its origin to the default path, but `/avatars/*` isn't a served route (only `/uploads/*` is). Removed the gorm default from `User.AvatarURL`; ran one-time SQL to clear existing literal defaults to empty string.

### Known Latent Issues (Not Blocking)

- **Privacy filter post-LIMIT** in `GetDiscoverFeed` ([posts.go:264-299](backend/internal/handlers/posts.go#L264-L299)) drops rows after the SQL `LIMIT` applies. With current data (mostly public-default settings) this is fine; if many users adopt `friends`/`only_me`, whole pages could get filtered to empty and the `hasMore = len > 0` heuristic would stop the feed prematurely. **Real fix:** move the privacy filter into SQL via `NOT EXISTS` / `EXISTS` joins against `user_settings` and `friendships`.
- **`GetLobbyChatFriendsHandler` raw SQL** ([lobby_chats.go:40-53](backend/internal/handlers/lobby_chats.go#L40-L53)) doesn't `SELECT users.avatar_url`. If this endpoint is ever consumed by the UI, avatars will be missing there. Fix: add `users.avatar_url` to the SELECT, or rewrite as a GORM query.
- **Soft-delete + local media files** — `DeletePost` soft-deletes the DB row and hard-deletes the CDN file (production), but **only** when the URL is absolute (`http://`/`https://`). Local-dev files (relative `/uploads/...` paths) are never deleted from disk → orphan files accumulate. For a "trash can" UX or GDPR compliance, add a deferred-purge job that hard-deletes posts (and their media) where `deleted_at` is older than N days.

### Avatar System Migration — Steps 2 + 3 (Completed May 11, 2026)

**Step 2 completed — consumers migrated to `<Avatar>`** (file:line per migration site):

- `DiscoverFeed.jsx` — post author avatar + comment author avatar
- `PostViewModal.jsx` — post author footer avatar
- `LobbyPage.jsx` — chat tab friend avatar (now also clickable lightbox), incoming friend request, sent friend request, selected chat user header
- `ChatHomeModal.jsx` — recent chats list
- `PrivateChatModal.jsx` — chat header
- `SessionChatPreviewModal.jsx` — chat message author
- `ContactsModal.jsx` — friends list (with lightbox), pending requests, sent requests
- `CallHistoryModal.jsx` — call history entry avatar
- `lobby/ActiveCallInterface.jsx` — minimized pill + full call avatar
- `lobby/IncomingCallModal.jsx` — caller avatar
- `lobby/OutgoingCallModal.jsx` — friend avatar
- `MembersModal.jsx` — member list
- `LectureHallMembersModal.jsx` — host badge + student rows
- `LobbyLeftSidebar.jsx` — current user header avatar
- `SettingsModal.jsx` — blocked users list
- `RoomPageEditModal.jsx` — host avatar (clickable) + inline member list (clickable to lightbox)

**Step 3 completed — backend handlers no longer build absolute URLs:**

- `friendships.go GetFriendsListHandler` — now returns raw `friend.AvatarURL` in both `avatar_url` and `profile_picture` keys (legacy alias).
- `user_profile.go GetUserProfileHandler` — returns raw `targetUser.AvatarURL`.
- `friendships.go GetBackendURL` — removed (no longer used).
- `"strings"` import removed from both files; `"os"` import removed from friendships.go.

**BunnyCDN safety verified:** absolute URLs (production CDN) pass through `resolveAvatarUrl` unchanged. Local `/uploads/...` paths get prefixed with `VITE_API_BASE_URL` by the frontend. `VITE_API_BASE_URL` must be set in Vercel for both prod and preview deploys.

**Not migrated (low-risk, follow-up):**

- `ProfilePage.jsx` — appears to be a stub; not in active routes.
- `RoomMembersModal.jsx` — already uses shadcn `Avatar` component with its own fallback.
- `cinema/ui/LiveShareManager.jsx` (2 sites) — deeply nested in cinema UI, deferred.
- `cinema/ui/LectureHallSeatsGrid.jsx` (2 sites) — uses absolute-positioned overlay on seat buttons; deferred.
- `cinema/3d-cinema/avatars/UserAvatar.jsx` — Three.js HTML overlay, not a regular `<img>`.
- `pages/AdminDashboard.jsx` (donor leaderboard) — admin-only, low traffic.
- `payment/DonateTokenToMember.jsx` — low visibility.

### UI Additions

- **Chat tab avatar lightbox** — clicking a friend avatar in the lobby chat tab opens a fullscreen lightbox with the larger image and the username overlay. State: `lightboxAvatarUser` in `LobbyPage.jsx`. Click event uses `stopPropagation` + `preventDefault` so it doesn't trigger the parent button's `handleOpenChat`.

### Discover Feed Loading Speed Optimizations

- **Backend N+1 fix** ([posts.go GetDiscoverFeed](backend/internal/handlers/posts.go)) — was running 1 `user_settings` SELECT per post in the loop (12 sequential queries per page just for privacy checks). Now batches all unique authors into a single `WHERE user_id IN (...)` query before filtering.
- **Frontend prefetch** — `DiscoverFeed.jsx` IntersectionObserver now uses `rootMargin: '600px'` so the next page request fires before the sentinel reaches the viewport. `PostsGrid.jsx` uses `rootMargin: '400px'` (smaller because it scrolls inside a modal). Net effect: next batch is in flight while the user is still scrolling through the current one, so older posts appear without the previous noticeable pause at the bottom.

