## 🔔 Social Graph & Notification Features (May 16, 2026)

### Strategic Context

Four social graph features were planned and implemented in priority order:

1. **Live-session alert to lobby members** — broadcast `session_started` WS event when host starts a session
2. **Persistent notification records** — notifications table, model, API, CreateNotification helper
3. **Lobby notification badge** — bell icon with unread count + dropdown panel in LobbyPage
4. **Following feed** — `GET /api/posts/following` endpoint + For You/Following pill toggle in Feed tab

### Feature 1 — Live-Session Alert ✅

When a host starts a session, `session_started` WebSocket event is broadcast to all lobby members of that room.

- `backend/internal/handlers/sessions.go` — after creating the DB session row, calls `hub.BroadcastToLobby(roomID, ...)` with `type: "session_started"` payload
- `frontend/src/components/LobbyPage.jsx` — listens on the lobby WS, shows a toast banner "🎬 [Host] started a session — Join Now" with a clickable link to the watch URL
- No new DB tables needed

### Feature 2 — Persistent Notification Records ✅

**New DB model & migration:**
- `backend/internal/models/notification.go` — `Notification` struct: `UserID`, `Type`, `Title`, `Body`, `EntityType`, `EntityID`, `IsRead`, `ReadAt`
- Migration: `backend/migrations/20260516_create_notifications.sql` — `notifications` table with `idx_notifications_user_unread` partial index on `(user_id, created_at DESC) WHERE is_read = false`
- AutoMigrate entry added in `backend/cmd/server/main.go`

**Helper function:**
```go
// backend/internal/handlers/notifications.go
func CreateNotification(userID uint, notifType, title, body, entityType string, entityID uint) {
    // Inserts DB row + pushes WS "notification" event to user
}
```

**Trigger points:**
- Session start → notifies all room members (called from `sessions.go`)
- New post in a room → notifies room members (called from `posts.go`)

**API endpoints** (registered under `protected` group):
- `GET /api/notifications?page=N&limit=20` — paginated list, newest first
- `PUT /api/notifications/read-all` — marks all unread as read, returns updated count
- `GET /api/notifications/count` — returns `{ unread_count: N }`

**Files modified:**
- `backend/internal/models/notification.go` (new)
- `backend/migrations/20260516_create_notifications.sql` (new)
- `backend/internal/handlers/notifications.go` (new — handler + CreateNotification helper)
- `backend/cmd/server/main.go` (AutoMigrate + 3 route registrations)
- `backend/internal/handlers/sessions.go` (calls CreateNotification on session start)
- `backend/internal/handlers/posts.go` (calls CreateNotification on new post + new `GetFollowingFeedHandler`)

### Feature 3 — Lobby Notification Badge ✅

Added to `frontend/src/components/LobbyPage.jsx`:

- `BellIcon`, `XMarkIcon` added to heroicons/24/solid imports
- State: `notifications`, `unreadNotifCount`, `showNotifPanel` (all pre-existing from Feature 2 WS push; `fetchNotifications` and `markAllNotifsRead` helpers added)
- **Bell button** — fixed top-right (`z-30`), shows red badge with count when `unreadNotifCount > 0`; clicking toggles the panel and marks all read
- **Notification panel** — `fixed top-16 right-4 z-40 w-80 max-h-96`, lists notifications with title/body/timestamp; unread rows highlighted with `bg-gray-800`

### Feature 4 — Following Feed ✅

**Backend** (`backend/internal/handlers/posts.go`):
- `GetFollowingFeedHandler` — `GET /api/posts/following`
- Fetches all `UserRoom` rows for the requesting user → extracts unique room host IDs → queries `posts WHERE user_id IN (hostIDs) AND is_public = true ORDER BY created_at DESC`
- Paginates with `?page=N&limit=20`; deduplicates host IDs via a map to handle multi-room hosts
- Wraps results through `buildPostResponse` (same as other feed handlers) — returns `{ posts, total, page }`
- Route registered in `postsProtected` group in `main.go`

**Frontend** (`frontend/src/components/LobbyPage.jsx`):
- "Discover" sub-tab renamed to "Feed" (both desktop and mobile buttons)
- `feedPill` state (`'for_you' | 'following'`) + `followingFeed` state (`{ posts, loading, page, total, initialized }`)
- `fetchFollowingFeed(page, append)` — lazy-loads on first pill activation, supports load-more
- Inside Feed tab: **For You / Following pill toggle** → For You renders existing `<DiscoverFeed>`, Following renders paginated post grid with load-more button
- useEffect triggers fetch on first switch to Following pill

### LiveShare Forced Mode — Content Rating Auto-Selection ✅

When a session has a specific content rating, the LiveShare wizard skips the mode-selection step and pre-selects the only valid mode:

| Content Rating | Forced Mode | Steps shown |
|---|---|---|
| `Religious` | `church` | Setup → Share Type → Layout |
| `Educational` | `regular` | Share Type → Layout |
| Any other | none | Mode → (Setup if applicable) → Share Type → Layout |

**Prop chain:** `LeftSidebar` (derives `contentRating` from `sessionStatus?.content_rating`) → `LiveShareManager` → `LiveShareWizard`

**`frontend/src/components/liveshare/LiveShareWizard.jsx`:**
- New `contentRating = ''` prop
- `const forcedMode = contentRating === 'Religious' ? 'church' : contentRating === 'Educational' ? 'regular' : null;`
- `selectedMode` state initialises to `forcedMode || null` (not `null`)
- `getSteps()` omits `{ id: 'mode' }` step when `forcedMode` is set
- `muteAllMembers` useEffect still fires normally — church mode auto-mutes all members on mount

**`frontend/src/components/cinema/ui/LiveShareManager.jsx`:**
- Added `contentRating = ''` to props destructuring
- Passes `contentRating={contentRating}` to `<LiveShareWizard>`

**`frontend/src/components/cinema/ui/LeftSidebar.jsx`:**
- `contentRating` was already derived at component level from `sessionStatus?.content_rating`
- Added `contentRating={contentRating}` to the `<LiveShareManager>` JSX

### Pending / Deferred

- **Room type system** — add `room_type` varchar field to Room model (`church`, `education`, `general`); room type selector in CreateNewModal; content rating auto-lock based on room type (discussed, not yet coded)
- **Gift → Offering renaming** — FloatingGiftIcon, DonationNotification, SessionEarningsModal: conditional labels when `room.content_rating === 'Religious'` (discussed, not yet coded)
- **User preferences in LobbyLeftSidebar** — new menu item opening preferences panel (preferred content categories, default content rating)
- **Save content rating on instant watch** — hook into PricingModal/AccessModal callbacks to persist last-used content rating to user preferences
- **Onboarding flow** — initial feed/category preferences screen; saves to user preferences

